# s6_onnx_initializer_release: each ONNX initializer dropped from the protobuf once it is a tensor.
#
# table      s5's peak (sample_ts_ms=1786959599921 sample_rss_kb=2057864 = peaks/PEAK):
#              867.0 MB  libstdc++.so.6.0.30+0xf4979   the protobuf parse            42.2% of the peak  <- RANK 1
#              433.5 MB  python3.10+0x13cc27           the ONNX byte buffer
#              433.0 MB  libc10.so+0x4a675             the tensors being built
#              --------
#              1733.5 MB of a 2055.2 MB peak, all three live at the SAME instant.
#            2x the 433 MB payload: numpy_helper.to_array returns fresh bytes for node.raw_data, the tensor
#            views them; each weight inside and outside the message until _to_crypten returns.
# replaces   plaintext_free_early_cpu (twice null on this base): the 433.0 MB libc10 row = new tensors
#            from_onnx builds, not the released model.
# free       raw_data unread once its tensor exists. Gate expected to pass exactly.
# expected   867.0 -> ~433 MB (up to -433 MB in conversion). Inference needs 1,750,020 / 1,781,740 /
#            1,790,984 kB with the arena returned (p_phases_pinned_s5): peak ~1.8 GB (~-12%), not lower;
#            below 1.75 GB = phase attribution wrong.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,onnx_initializer_release_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
